{#-
  Organization logo tile for the homepage organizations marquee.

  The Sanity logos are opaque 16:9 brand tiles, so the atom mutes them
  (grayscale, lowered opacity) and restores colour on hover. Alt text is the
  organization name: that is what the logo communicates, and the Sanity
  `logo.alt` values are inconsistent ("QVC Company Logo", null, …).

  Falls back to the plain title when an organization has no logo.

Params:
  title    string  Organization name. Trimmed; used as the alt text.
  logo     object  Sanity logo: { asset: { url, metadata.dimensions } }.
  classes  string  Appended to the img classes through the `classes` filter.
-#}
{% macro render(params = {}) %}
  {%- set title = params.title | default('Untitled organization') | trim -%}
  {%- set asset = params.logo.asset if params.logo else null -%}
  {%- set dimensions = asset.metadata.dimensions if (asset and asset.metadata) else null -%}

  {%- set styles = {
    "base": "block w-32 h-auto grayscale opacity-60 transition-[filter,opacity] duration-(--transition-duration-base) ease-(--ease-standard) hover:grayscale-0 hover:opacity-100 motion-reduce:transition-none",
    "md": "w-40"
  } -%}

  {%- if asset and asset.url -%}
    <img src="{{ asset.url | imageUrl({w: 320, q: 75}) }}"
         alt="{{ title }}"
         width="{{ dimensions.width if dimensions else 320 }}"
         height="{{ dimensions.height if dimensions else 180 }}"
         loading="lazy"
         decoding="async"
         class="{{ [styles, params.classes] | classes }}" />
  {%- else -%}
    {{ title }}
  {%- endif -%}
{% endmacro %}
